    "basmil_image_text_Ya7NUt": {
      "type": "basmil-image-text",
      "blocks": {
        "content_zABD7A": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is <brown>Shilajit</brown>?",
            "subtitle": "",
            "description": "<p><a href=\"https://everestshilajit.com/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"shilajit\">Shilajit</a> is not just another typical supplement-it’s darker, richer, more potent, straight from the Himalayas and whatnot. It’s fully loaded with 85+ minerals from the Himalayan soil and different bioactive compounds, products of microbial decomposition.</p><p>Only found in the high-altitude regions of the Himalayas, Shilajit is a tar-like blackish resin oozing out from the crevices of the rocks. Ayurveda recognizes it as a destroyer of weakness and conqueror of mountains, a superfood used for over &gt;3000 years.</p><p>What sets Shilajit apart is the extraordinary concentration of <a href=\"https://everestshilajit.com/pages/fulvic-and-humic-acids\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"humic and fulvic acid\">humic and fulvic acid</a> (60%+), humic acid, and over 85 <a href=\"https://everestshilajit.com/pages/trace-minerals\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"trace minerals\">trace minerals</a> present in it, in their bioavailable form. It's nowhere near other synthetic supplements- its formation is completely natural, created through centuries of plant decomposition and compression.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_text_2": "",
            "button_link_2": ""
          }
        }
      },
