    "faq_PQHLLV": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "text_naRTYA": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Shilajit?",
            "answer": "<p>Shilajit is a miracle from nature, a medicine of Ayurveda for &gt;3000 years and a multi-mineral natural supplement all parts of the world use today.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_ApeTQV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does fulvic acid do?",
            "answer": "<p>Fulvic acid is a product of the decomposition of plants after a long time of breakage and decay by soil microorganisms. Taken orally, it functions as a chelator and enhances absorption of minerals, trace elements and other nutrients, especially useful during treatment of deficiencies.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_XA3rxm": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the best benefits of Shilajit?",
            "answer": "<p>There are various benefits behind the celebration of shilajit in traditional medicine and modern medicine: energy, endurance, mental clarity, focus, reproductive health improvement, strengthened immune function and detoxification being the major ones.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_wnpiM4": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is Shilajit different from regular supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>Shilajit is not an ordinary supplement -it is a rare natural secretion of Himalaya. It has 85+ minerals and beneficial compounds like fulvic acid; making its use applicable for more than one impairment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_QKGypJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is pure Shilajit more expensive than regular supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>Firstly, shilajit is geographically limited to the higher altitudes, and additionally, its formation takes centuries. So, you can imagine how expensive it can get after further going through multiple purification processes.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_agCQ3N": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I know if Shilajit is authentic?",
            "answer": "<p>An authentic shilajit should exactly be: darker, tar-like, and smell similar to a cow’s stale urine. Moreover, it should fully dissolve in water and shouldn’t catch fire.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_hdLUbV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take Shilajit with other supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, you can. Shilajit gives combined benefits when taken with other supplements.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_WiWyE9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does it take to see results?",
            "answer": "<p>In those who have continuity, shilajit has been seen to be effective after two to four weeks. For optimum benefits, consume it for about 48 weeks.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
